Subject: ntdll: disable the lsteamclient bridge by default on macOS

Proton redirects steamclient64.dll's and gameoverlayrenderer64.dll's tier0_s64 /
vstdlib_s64 imports to ntdll so its Linux host-integrated tier0 shims serve
games. That bridge cannot reach a Linux Steam on macOS, and against the real
Windows Steam client the redirect strands g_pMemAllocSteam and friends on
unimplemented ntdll stubs -- this fork's de-linux'd ntdll lacks those 297 symbols
-- so steamclient64's DllMain access-violates on a garbage allocator vtable and
Steam offers to reinstall itself.

Whisky set PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT=1 on every launch to get here. A constant
in the launcher's environment is a constant every harness standing in for a GUI
launch has to mirror by hand, and those mirrors drift: steam-startup-loop.sh was
already missing a different one. The default belongs in the code that reads it.

PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT=0 restores upstream behaviour.

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
index c06e82b4e84..ea1c254c294 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/loader.c
@@ -1156,7 +1156,12 @@ static int use_lsteamclient(void)
 
     if (use != -1) return use;
 
-    use = !get_env( L"PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT", env, sizeof(env) ) || *env == '0';
+    /* Off unless PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT=0 asks for it. The bridge redirects
+     * steamclient64/gameoverlayrenderer64 imports to Proton's Linux-host tier0
+     * shims, which can never reach a Linux Steam on macOS -- and against the real
+     * Windows client it strands g_pMemAllocSteam on ntdll stubs this fork does not
+     * have, so steamclient64's DllMain access-violates and Steam says "reinstall". */
+    use = get_env( L"PROTON_DISABLE_LSTEAMCLIENT", env, sizeof(env) ) && *env == '0';
     if (!use)
         ERR("lsteamclient disabled.\n");
     return use;
